Description: Disable PrefersExternalSampler on Linux V4L2 decode path
 .
 On Raspberry Pi 5 with Linux >= 6.18 the V4L2 stateless HEVC decoder
 advertises V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_COL128 (multi-planar SAND128) as the
 preferred 8-bit output format. When chromium asks Mesa v3d to import
 such a buffer as a single multi-plane EGLImage with the OES external
 sampler, it samples as solid green RGB(0,136,0) - the underlying NV12
 data is never read. mpv works because its dmabuf_interop_gl always
 splits NV12 buffers into two single-plane EGLImages (R8 for Y, GR88
 for UV) regardless of single- vs multi-planar V4L2 origin.
 .
 PrefersExternalSampler=true is what routes our NV12 frames to that
 broken single-EGLImage code path in OzoneImageGLTexturesHolder. With
 the flag false, chromium imports the two V4L2 planes as separate
 R8 + GR88 GL_TEXTURE_2D textures, matching mpv's working pattern.
 .
 The flag is mainly an efficiency hint for ChromeOS - Linux Chromium
 with V4L2 hwdec is a Pi-only path for us, so unconditionally
 disabling external sampler on Linux is safe.
 .
 References:
   - https://github.com/sslivins/chromium-rpi-hevc/issues/41
   - kernel commit raspberrypi/linux@2953bb2d91 (the regression)
   - https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/blob/master/video/out/hwdec/dmabuf_interop_gl.c
Author: Stephen Slivinski <stesli@>
Last-Update: 2026-05-22

--- a/media/gpu/chromeos/mailbox_video_frame_converter.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/chromeos/mailbox_video_frame_converter.cc
@@ -249,9 +249,17 @@ MailboxVideoFrameConverter::GenerateSharedImage(
                            VideoPixelFormatToString(origin_frame->format()));
     return nullptr;
   }
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
-  // If format is true multiplanar format, we prefer external sampler on
-  // ChromeOS and Linux.
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
+  // If format is true multiplanar format, we prefer external sampler on
+  // ChromeOS.
+  //
+  // PATCH_NO_EXT_SAMPLER_LINUX: do NOT request external sampler on Linux.
+  // On Raspberry Pi 5 (kernel >= 6.18 with V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_COL128),
+  // importing multi-planar SAND128 buffers as a single multi-plane EGLImage
+  // with an OES sampler renders solid green. Forcing the per-plane path
+  // (R8 + GR88 single-plane EGLImages with GL_TEXTURE_2D) matches mpv's
+  // working dmabuf_interop_gl pattern and is robust across both
+  // NV12_COL128 and NV12MT_COL128 V4L2 outputs.
   if (si_format->is_multi_plane()) {
     si_format->SetPrefersExternalSampler();
   }
